  "glass industry terminology": "terminologi industri kaca",
  "Glass is bought on sheets and priced by area, and those buy prices change. When they do, every stored quotation that recalculates itself silently becomes a different quotation. If your profitability reporting reads those figures, your historical margin data is rewritten every time a supplier changes a rate.": "Kaca dibeli dalam bentuk lembaran dan diberi harga berdasarkan area, dan harga beli tersebut berubah. Ketika hal ini terjadi, setiap kutipan tersimpan yang menghitung ulang dirinya sendiri secara diam-diam menjadi kutipan yang berbeda. Jika laporan profitabilitas Anda menunjukkan angka tersebut, data margin historis Anda ditulis ulang setiap kali pemasok mengubah tarif.",
  "Glass is quoted by area, not by piece. The industry unit is the square metre (SQM), and pieces are described in millimetres: W for width, H for height. A unit with two different panes needs both, which is why quotations often show W1 / H1 / W2 / H2 — the outer pane and the inner pane measured separately. Linear metres (LM) appear where an edge treatment is priced by the length of edge rather than by area.": "Kaca dikutip berdasarkan area, bukan per bagian. Satuan industrinya adalah meter persegi (SQM), dan satuannya dinyatakan dalam milimeter: W untuk lebar, H untuk tinggi. Unit dengan dua panel berbeda memerlukan keduanya, itulah sebabnya kutipan sering kali menunjukkan W1 / H1 / W2 / H2 — panel luar dan panel dalam diukur secara terpisah. Meter linier (LM) muncul ketika perlakuan tepi diberi harga berdasarkan panjang tepi, bukan berdasarkan luas.",
